                <pb facs="0847" n="777" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg777"/>

                <head>Mr. Hovey to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 91.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States, Lima,
                                Peru,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-09-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 28, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On the 22d instant a very serious outbreak
                    took place in Arequipa, (following that mentioned in my despatch No. 90, of the
                    22d instant,) in which all the military stationed in that city took part with
                    the populace against the government, and remained, at last advices, masters of
                    the situation. General Canseco, vice-president under General Pezet, has assumed
                    command of the revolutionary forces, and declared himself constitutional chief
                    of the republic.</p>
                <p>Troops have been despatched from Lima to quell this insurrection, and if they
                    remain faithful to President Prado will, I have no doubt, be successful.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ALVIN P. HOVEY.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
